@startuml
title OO Abuser: Switch Statements -- AFTER (Refactored)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #D4EDDA
skinparam ClassBorderColor #28A745
skinparam ClassFontSize 13
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 12

note "REFACTORED: Replace Conditional\nwith Polymorphism" as N1 #69DB7C

abstract class Employee <<Clean Code>> {
  - name : String
  - monthlySalary : double
  --
  + getMonthlySalary() : double
  + {abstract} calculatePay() : double
  + {abstract} getVacationDays() : int
}

class Engineer <<Clean Code>> {
  + calculatePay() : double
  .. return getMonthlySalary() ..
  + getVacationDays() : int
  .. return 15 ..
}

class Salesman <<Clean Code>> {
  - commission : double
  --
  + calculatePay() : double
  .. return getMonthlySalary() + commission ..
  + getVacationDays() : int
  .. return 12 ..
}

class Manager <<Clean Code>> {
  - bonus : double
  --
  + calculatePay() : double
  .. return getMonthlySalary() + bonus ..
  + getVacationDays() : int
  .. return 20 ..
}

Employee <|-- Engineer
Employee <|-- Salesman
Employee <|-- Manager

N1 .. Employee

note bottom of Employee
  <color:#28A745><b>Benefits:</b></color>
  - No switch statements needed
  - Adding new type = new subclass (Open/Closed)
  - Each class encapsulates its own behavior
  - No duplicated conditional logic
end note

@enduml
